      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-211992",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 8{x}^{3}\\,{7}^{5{x}^{4}+8}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=5{x}^{4}+8.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{20}\\text{d}u={x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}\\,{7}^{5{x}^{4}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8\\cdot {7}^{5{x}^{4}+8}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {7}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int {7}^{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {7}^{u}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {7}^{5{x}^{4}+8}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
