      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73799",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 4{x}^{2}{5}^{{x}^{3}+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={x}^{3}+2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{x}^{2}{5}^{{x}^{3}+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {5}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int {5}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\frac{{5}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+2}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
  ],
  "canonical_example": {
    ":db/id": 17592186183946,
    ":question/id": "ab4772a2-f980-5ad7-a377-34e34b95be83",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-14403",
    ":question/problem": "Calculate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u= 1-x^4.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\textrm{d}u}{ \\textrm{d}x} = -4x^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int {x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} }\\, \\textrm{d}x \n&=\\int {{3^{1-x^4}}\\cdot x^3 }\\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt]\n&=  \\int {3^{u}} \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) \\textrm{d}u\\\\[5pt]\n                                                     &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\int {3^{u}}  \\textrm{d}u\\\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=  -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C\\\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=   -\\dfrac{3^{1-x^4}}{4\\ln 3}+ C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
